# Commit after every change

For this repository, **commit after each logical change** — even small fixes, hotfixes, config tweaks, or rule updates. Do not batch unrelated work into one commit.

## When to commit

- After finishing any edit that builds or affects runtime behavior
- After deploy-related script/rule changes
- One commit per focused change (not one giant end-of-session dump)

## How to commit

Follow git safety protocol:

- Run `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -1` before committing
- Never skip hooks, never amend unless protocol allows
- Use a clear 1–2 sentence message focused on **why**
- Do **not** push unless the user asks

## Scope note

This project rule **overrides** “only commit when explicitly asked” for NewTerraforged work.
